{"name":"Electric Ultramarine","hex":"#3f00ff","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"electric","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, produced by, operated with, or utilising electricity; electrical.","Of or relating to an electronic version of a musical instrument that has an acoustic equivalent."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electricity; the electricity supply.","An electric powered version of something that was originally or is more commonly not electric."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electric"},{"term":"ultramarine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Beyond the sea.","Of a brilliant dark blue or slightly purplish color like that of the pigment (noun sense 1)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["In full ultramarine blue: a brilliant blue pigment traditionally made from ground-up lapis lazuli, and now usually either extracted from mineral deposits or made synthetically.","A brilliant dark blue or slightly purplish colour like that of the pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ultramarine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ultramarine","blocks":[{"text":"Ultramarine is a deep blue pigment historically derived from lazurite, the principal component of the metamorphic rock lapis lazuli. The pigment was produced by grinding the stone and undergoing a complex washing process to isolate the blue mineral, which made it exceptionally valuable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ultramarinepigment.jpg/330px-Ultramarinepigment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultramarine","wikidata":"Q219660"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ultramarinepigment.jpg/500px-Ultramarinepigment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ultramarinep